Create a file named .mcp.json at the PROJECT ROOT (committed to version control = 'project scope'). Schema is a top-level mcpServers object keyed by server name. For a stdio server the fields are: type:"stdio", command (executable), args (string array), env (object). Example committed to the repo root:

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "serena": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["--from","git+https://github.com/oraios/serena","serena","start-mcp-server","--context","ide-assistant","--project","${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}"],
      "env": {}
    }
  }
}

Key official details: (1) The official minimal project-scope example shown in the docs omits even type and just uses command/args/env { "mcpServers": { "shared-server": { "command": "/path/to/server", "args": [], "env": {} } } } — type defaults to stdio. (2) Equivalent CLI that writes this file for you: `claude mcp add --scope project --transport stdio serena -- uvx ...` (ALL flags must come BEFORE the name; `--` separates name from the server command). (3) Env-var expansion is supported in command/args/env/url/headers via ${VAR} and ${VAR:-default}. (4) CRITICAL for project scope: ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} is set in the SERVER's env, not Claude Code's own, so when you reference it inside a project-scoped .mcp.json command/args you MUST give a default: ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}. (5) Project-scoped servers from .mcp.json require one-time approval ('Pending approval' in `claude mcp list`); reset with `claude mcp reset-project-choices`. This satisfies the HARD project-only constraint: nothing touches ~/.claude.json or other projects.
